WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:22.008
frowned as a female member of the Red Council droned on about election details.

2
00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:26.351
The businessman had wandered to the back of the room ten minutes earlier.

3
00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:28.513
He glanced toward the group.

4
00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:32.696
Boz was sitting up front with his non-Red daughter and her husband.

5
00:00:33.716 --> 00:00:37.497
All three were listening carefully to what the Red Council member was saying.

6
00:00:38.397 --> 00:00:43.399
Laddno glared at Boz, but the old Magic Master didn't even look his way.

7
00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:45.739
Laddno began pacing.

8
00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:50.821
He didn't like being ignored, especially by a bunch of snooty Reds and their cronies.

9
00:00:51.861 --> 00:00:53.881
But that would all change soon.

10
00:00:54.522 --> 00:00:58.463
Once he was elected king, Laddno planned to make some big changes.

11
00:00:59.463 --> 00:01:03.164
He'd start by hanging an enormous portrait of himself in the palace.

12
00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:07.517
Then no one could ignore him—or his power!

13
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:13.519
He was thinking about what color to paint the throne room when the familiar pain filled his head

14
00:01:13.559 --> 00:01:17.560
again. He held his head and staggered out of the room.

15
00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.901
He collapsed against the wall, panting as the pain subsided slightly.

16
00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:25.602
The voice in his head spoke.

17
00:01:26.822 --> 00:01:28.282
"What?" Laddno replied.

18
00:01:28.302 --> 00:01:29.303
"How soon?"

19
00:01:30.403 --> 00:01:32.164
He paused and listened again.

20
00:01:32.664 --> 00:01:33.724
Then he frowned.

21
00:01:34.872 --> 00:01:36.193
"Are you sure they're really coming?"

22
00:01:36.493 --> 00:01:37.194
Laddno asked.

23
00:01:37.214 --> 00:01:38.734
"What if they can't do it?"

24
00:01:39.735 --> 00:01:43.037
Once again he fell silent as the voice raged on.

25
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:45.118
Finally Laddno nodded.

26
00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.040
"All right," he said resolutely.

27
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.801
"I'll begin immediately."

28
00:01:49.821 --> 00:01:57.005
"Hold still," a Niffian said as he dabbed purple goo on Zann's fingers.

29
00:01:57.946 --> 00:02:01.628
Perda stared at her own fingers, which were already coated with the stuff.

30
00:02:02.644 --> 00:02:04.125
"How does this work again?"

31
00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:04.826
she asked.

32
00:02:04.846 --> 00:02:10.990
"This oogberry paste will work with your magical friction," the Niffian explained.

33
00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.453
"All you need to do is think of the place you wish to visit.

34
00:02:15.874 --> 00:02:19.556
When the paste glows, it means you're near your destination."

35
00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:22.779
"That sounds sort of like the guidelink."

36
00:02:23.079 --> 00:02:26.041
Gliss glanced at the device sticking out of Zann's pocket.

37
00:02:26.061 --> 00:02:29.904
"With that, we need to think about a certain type of magic."

38
00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:31.969
The Niffian smiled.

39
00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:36.391
"With the paste, you just need to think of a person or place."

40
00:02:36.411 --> 00:02:39.953
"That will make things easier," Zann said.

41
00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:41.494
He looked at his hands.

42
00:02:41.514 --> 00:02:43.235
"Okay, I think we're ready."

43
00:02:44.195 --> 00:02:46.516
He was grateful to the Niffians for helping them.

44
00:02:47.497 --> 00:02:51.699
But he was eager to get away from their stinky world as soon as possible.

45
00:02:51.979 --> 00:02:54.421
Besides, he was worried about Ello.

46
00:02:56.202 --> 00:02:58.723
Soon Zann and his friends were back in the vortex.

47
00:02:58.743 --> 00:03:01.833
"Think about Skellia, everyone!"

48
00:03:02.053 --> 00:03:02.653
Perda called.

49
00:03:05.954 --> 00:03:08.355
Within seconds the paste began to glow.

50
00:03:09.316 --> 00:03:11.176
Zann spotted an approaching wormhole.

51
00:03:11.196 --> 00:03:13.277
"That must be Skellia up ahead!"

52
00:03:13.437 --> 00:03:13.938
he shouted.

53
00:03:15.118 --> 00:03:19.140
Moments later they plunged through the wormhole and into cold water.

54
00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.442
The water was so rough, Zann was glad that the Shackle spell was holding them all together.

55
00:03:25.462 --> 00:03:28.424
Suddenly something large glided past beneath them.

56
00:03:29.556 --> 00:03:30.337
"A gulper!"

57
00:03:30.397 --> 00:03:31.037
Perda yelled.

58
00:03:31.057 --> 00:03:32.698
"Quick, inflate the boat!"

59
00:03:34.699 --> 00:03:36.620
Darb spit out a mouthful of water.

60
00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:42.603
Then he pulled down the boat, which had been draped over his shoulders, and yanked the little tab.

61
00:03:43.444 --> 00:03:45.485
Soon the boat was bobbing on the waves.

62
00:03:45.945 --> 00:03:47.846
By now the gulper had moved away.

63
00:03:48.406 --> 00:03:49.247
Zann was relieved.

64
00:03:50.147 --> 00:03:53.509
Since they hadn't used magic, the creature hadn't been interested in them.

65
00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:59.900
When they were all on the boat, Zann collapsed and caught his breath.

66
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.601
"We did it," he said.

67
00:04:01.621 --> 00:04:03.882
"Thanks to the Niffians."

68
00:04:04.342 --> 00:04:05.503
Perda looked at her hand.

69
00:04:05.523 --> 00:04:07.924
"My oogberry paste washed off."

70
00:04:07.944 --> 00:04:10.965
"Mine too," Gliss said.

71
00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:15.367
Zann saw that his fingers had also returned to their normal color.

72
00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:17.127
"Oh well.

73
00:04:17.888 --> 00:04:20.709
Hopefully the guidelink will help us find our way back to Magica."

74
00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:23.770
"First we have to find Ello," Darb said.

75
00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.451
Zann sat up and looked around.

76
00:04:26.871 --> 00:04:31.818
From horizon to horizon, all he could see were churning gray waves.

77
00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:34.801
There was no sign of land anywhere.

78
00:04:35.181 --> 00:04:36.462
Gliss peered at her hand.

79
00:04:36.482 --> 00:04:40.045
"Maybe there's some oogberry paste stuck under our fingernails."

80
00:04:40.065 --> 00:04:43.388
"I have a better idea," Perda said.

81
00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:45.850
"Let's use the guidelink.

82
00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.913
Since it tracks magic, we might be able to find Ello with it.

83
00:04:50.854 --> 00:04:56.358
We just need to focus on whatever type of magic Ello is using to communicate with Zann."

84
00:04:57.099 --> 00:04:58.020
Gliss frowned.

85
00:04:58.244 --> 00:05:00.445
"But we don't know what type that is."

86
00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:03.646
"It's worth a try," Zann said.

87
00:05:04.487 --> 00:05:06.848
He rubbed the guidelink and focused on Ello.

88
00:05:07.848 --> 00:05:11.710
He thought about the magic that Ello had used during their last visit to Skellia.

89
00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:13.951
At first nothing happened.

90
00:05:14.391 --> 00:05:19.513
So Perda and Gliss put their hands on the guidelink too and added their own thoughts to Zann's.

91
00:05:21.474 --> 00:05:23.355
Finally something tugged on the boat.

92
00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:25.676
"I think it's working!"

93
00:05:25.916 --> 00:05:26.516
Perda cried.

94
00:05:27.648 --> 00:05:30.770
The boat floated along, pulled by the guidelink's magic.

95
00:05:31.711 --> 00:05:33.892
Suddenly a gulper rose out of the water!

96
00:05:33.912 --> 00:05:35.534
"Oh, no!"

97
00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:36.374
Gliss wailed.

98
00:05:36.394 --> 00:05:38.916
"The guidelink attracted a gulper!"

99
00:05:38.936 --> 00:05:43.479
"Everyone, stop using magic," Darb called out.

100
00:05:43.499 --> 00:05:47.502
"Let's just sit here until the gulper swims away."

101
00:05:48.563 --> 00:05:50.704
When the gulper was gone, they tried again.

102
00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:57.204
Two more gulpers appeared, drawn by the energy of the guidelink.

103
00:05:57.224 --> 00:05:58.305
"What are we going to do?"

104
00:05:58.565 --> 00:05:59.065
Gliss said.

105
00:05:59.085 --> 00:06:00.727
"This isn't working!"

106
00:06:00.747 --> 00:06:04.269
"Let's try once more," Perda suggested.

107
00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:07.191
"This time, don't focus on Ello.

108
00:06:07.531 --> 00:06:10.854
Just think about finding the strongest magic source around."

109
00:06:11.894 --> 00:06:12.855
She looked at Zann.

110
00:06:12.875 --> 00:06:15.557
"Your parents said it could do that, right?"

111
00:06:15.577 --> 00:06:18.099
"I think so," Zann said.

112
00:06:18.119 --> 00:06:19.199
"Let's try it."

113
00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.402
This time the guidelink responded almost immediately.

114
00:06:23.802 --> 00:06:25.404
The boat sped over the waves.

115
00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:27.933
"Whoa!" Perda cried.

116
00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:30.134
"Wow," Darb said.

117
00:06:30.154 --> 00:06:33.477
"The guidelink must have found a really strong power source!"

118
00:06:34.838 --> 00:06:36.799
"Yeah," Zann said slowly.

119
00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:38.381
"That's weird though.

120
00:06:38.721 --> 00:06:41.223
I thought Skellia didn't have much native magic."

121
00:06:41.243 --> 00:06:43.524
"Look!" Perda shouted.

122
00:06:43.544 --> 00:06:44.565
"It's another boat."

123
00:06:45.626 --> 00:06:47.467
Zann peered through the sea spray.

124
00:06:47.948 --> 00:06:50.049
Something was bobbing on the waves up ahead.

125
00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.392
When they got closer, he laughed with relief.

126
00:06:54.408 --> 00:06:58.673
It was a rickety houseboat with a small figure waving to them from the deck.

127
00:06:58.693 --> 00:07:00.395
"It's Ello!"

128
00:07:00.535 --> 00:07:01.056
he cried.

129
00:07:01.076 --> 00:07:02.637
"We found him!"
